// ------------------------------------------------------------
// WRITTEN ANSWERS
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Q1: Name two rules in this project that a validator cannot express.
// A validator only looks at one document at a time, so it cannot check that
// doctorId points to a user that really exists and has the role "doctor"
// (or that patientId points to a patient). It also cannot make email unique
// across all users - that needs a unique index, not a validator.

// Q2: What is the difference between validationLevel strict and moderate,
// and when would you start with moderate?
// "strict" checks every insert and every update. "moderate" checks inserts
// and updates of documents that are already valid, but skips updates of old
// documents that already break the rules. I would start with moderate when
// adding a validator to a collection that already has old data, so the app
// keeps working while the old documents are found and fixed.

